```c
void swap_broken(int a, int b) {    /* a, b are copies. */
    int t = a; a = b; b = t;         /* caller never sees this. */
}

void swap(int *a, int *b) {          /* copies of two addresses. */
    int t = *a;
    *a = *b;                         /* writes the caller's objects. */
    *b = t;
}

void repoint(int *p, int *other) {
    p = other;                       /* only the local copy of p changes. */
}

int main(void) {
    int x = 1, y = 2;
    swap_broken(x, y);               /* x = 1, y = 2. */
    swap(&x, &y);                    /* x = 2, y = 1. */
    return 0;
}
```

| Inside the function | Caller sees a change? |
|---|---|
| `a = 5;` (int parameter). | no. |
| `*p = 5;` (write through pointer). | yes: the pointed-to object. |
| `p = other;` (reassign pointer). | no: the caller's pointer is unchanged. |

